    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by two elite-tier starts against Logan Gilbert. **Trea Turner** leads the charge with an 81.27 efficiency score, benefiting immensely from an 8% lineup order boost and a favorable matchup against an opposing arm with a 5.89 xERA. Matching him in upside is **Kyle Schwarber**, who carries a 79.42 score into the leadoff spot; both players are prime candidates for multi-hit games given the expansive park factors and the exploitable nature of the opposition. **Junior Caminero** remains a critical piece of the core, hitting cleanup with a 70.37 rating, as his efficiency holds steady despite a slightly tougher matchup against Sandy Alcantara. \n\nOn the periphery of the lineup, **Carson Benge** (67.24) and **Gary Sanchez** (66.22) offer strong platoon-adjusted value, with the latter capitalizing on a favorable park factor and a 4.35 xERA opponent. The most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer was the exclusion of **Caleb Durbin** (45.64). While he carries a desirable skill set, the combination of a high-difficulty opponent in Schlittler and a drop-off in order placement pushed his efficiency below the threshold for a start. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.78), whose leadoff potential is tempered by the risk of facing a strong arm in Trevor McDonald and a notable negative wind factor. We must remain cautious with **Yordan Alvarez** (57.10) today; while his xwOBA is elite, the negative platoon split and a tough matchup against Jump suggest he is a start that relies more on his raw talent than a favorable tactical environment. Managers should ensure the final lineups confirm **Casey Schmitt**, **Carson Benge**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** in the leadoff spots as projected; any significant shuffle in the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores.",
